<title>BRAZIL: Brazil aluminium output up marginally in 1996.</title>
<headline>Brazil aluminium output up marginally in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's production of primary aluminium totalled 1.2 million tonnes in 1996, the Brazilian Aluminium Association (ABAL) said in a statement.</p>
<p>This was was 0.6 percent higher than 1995 output of 1.19 million tonnes and within ABAL predictions, it added.</p>
<p>Output in December reached 101,000 tonnes, a drop of one percent on the 102,000 produced in the same month in 1995.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
